					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: DRAWING LINES BETWEEN POINTS (ADVANCED)\n\nIn this example we are generating a float 2 collection with 10 values using Perlin Generator and Linear (like in the previous example).\nThis collection gets used for the begin position of each line.\n\nNext, we take this collection and shift all values by one.\nIndex 0 becomes 1, index 1 becomes 2 and so on, it does wrap.\n\nTo prevent the final entry drawing a line to the first entry we read the first entry and overwrite the shifted collection at index 0 with that value."
					}
				},
